#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Control modes"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-modes
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"Many hybrid inverters have a “Control Mode” setting: GoodWe, SMA STP SE, "
"Fronius Gen24, Kostal Plenticore, SolarEdge and Sungrow. Hybrid inverters "
"usually have their own self-consumption control. The control mode determines "
"who controls:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Mode\n"
"| Effect\n"
"| Prerequisite\n"
"\n"
"| **INTERNAL**\n"
"| The inverter controls itself (self-consumption or automatic mode). OpenEMS does **not** specify any power.\n"
"| Manufacturer's meter at the grid connection\n"
"| **SMART**\n"
"| The inverter controls in automatic mode. OpenEMS only intervenes if a function requires something else, e.g. charging from the grid or discharge lock.\n"
"| Manufacturer's meter at the grid connection\n"
"| **REMOTE**\n"
"| OpenEMS specifies the power completely. According to the code, slower than the internal mode.\n"
"| no manufacturer's meter necessary\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"Not every driver has all three modes. **Important:** With `+GoodWe.Ess+`, "
"Fronius Gen24, Kostal Plenticore and SolarEdge, the mode is set to INTERNAL "
"ex works. As long as it is not changed, xref:user/storage-control/time-of-"
"use-tariffs.adoc[price control], emergency reserve, etc. have no effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "GoodWe in FENECON Home and Commercial"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-goodwe-in-fenecon-home-and-commercial
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"Control is most extensive with GoodWe (see also xref:user/systems/fenecon-"
"home.adoc[FENECON Home]). The system apps set up the inverter, battery, "
"storage and PV inputs in one step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Inverter\n"
"| Series\n"
"| System\n"
"\n"
"| FENECON FHI 10 DAH\n"
"| ET\n"
"| Home 10\n"
"| FENECON ET Gen2 6K / 10K / 15K\n"
"| EUB\n"
"| Home 6, Home 10 Gen2, Home 15\n"
"| FENECON FHI 20 DAH / FHI 30 DAH\n"
"| ETT\n"
"| Home 20, Home 30\n"
"| FENECON 50K\n"
"| ETF\n"
"| Commercial 50 Gen3\n"
"| FENECON 100K\n"
"| NBC\n"
"| Commercial 100\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"In addition, the driver recognizes the GoodWe devices GW5K/8K/10K of the ET "
"series (hybrid) and BT series (battery inverter, see below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"**Control mode:** **SMART** ex works; the system apps do not change it. "
"OpenEMS therefore only intervenes if a function requires it, e.g. price "
"control, emergency reserve or xref:user/storage-control/section-14a-"
"enwg.adoc[§ 14a]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"**Other settings on the inverter** (according to the settings of the "
"component): feed-in limit (from the system settings or from the xref:user/"
"storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc[ripple control receiver]), "
"emergency power output, shadow management of the PV inputs and grid "
"connection rules (country code, VDE 4105, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid "**Start/stop:** AUTO ex works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "GoodWe BT series"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-goodwe-bt-series
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"The GoodWe devices of the BT series are battery inverters **without PV "
"inputs**. They only charge the battery via the alternating current side. The "
"code has **no separate treatment** for them: wherever the driver "
"distinguishes by device type, BT and ET are treated the same. Differences "
"only arise from the fact that no PV inputs are set up on the BT:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Point\n"
"| ET (hybrid)\n"
"| BT (without PV inputs)\n"
"\n"
"| PV inputs in the configuration\n"
"| `+GoodWe.Charger…+`\n"
"| none (do not tick “Has DC-PV 1 (MPPT 1)” and “Has DC-PV 2 (MPPT 2)” in the app)\n"
"| Storage power at the grid\n"
"| Battery plus PV power\n"
"| battery power only\n"
"| Maximum charging power from the grid\n"
"| maximum battery charging power minus current PV power\n"
"| full battery charging power (limited by inverter and battery)\n"
"| Charging specification from OpenEMS\n"
"| Charge battery with specification plus PV power\n"
"| Charge battery exactly with the specification\n"
"| Surplus feed-in (PV power that the full battery can no longer absorb)\n"
"| is calculated\n"
"| not applicable\n"
"| Feed-in limit\n"
"| the driver `+GoodWe.Ess+` does not set one; setting on the inverter\n"
"| not applicable; the PV system has its own inverter\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid "The behavior is therefore suitable for a battery inverter. Note:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"**Control mode:** `+GoodWe.Ess+` is set to INTERNAL ex works, and the app "
"“FENECON Pro Hybrid GW” does not change this. The inverter then controls "
"itself and OpenEMS does not control the storage. For price control, "
"emergency reserve, etc. to take effect, the mode must be set to SMART or "
"REMOTE."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"**Own control:** In INTERNAL or SMART mode, the BT controls according to its "
"own grid meter. This records the entire feed-in, including that of the "
"separate PV inverter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"Whether a BT implements the charging and discharging commands in the same "
"way as an ET cannot be determined from the code. This would have to be "
"checked on the device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other special features"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-other-special-features
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"**Kostal Plenticore:** Small setpoints around 0 W are set to 0 W (tolerance "
"band) so that the storage does not constantly switch between charging and "
"discharging with small grid fluctuations. An unchanged setpoint is only "
"rewritten at intervals of the set watchdog interval. OpenEMS cannot limit "
"the PV power of the Plenticore."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-other-special-features
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"**KACO blueplanet hybrid 10:** From firmware version 8, the inverter ignores "
"setpoints as long as the default password is set. OpenEMS reports this as a "
"warning. The PV power can be limited via the component "
"`+Kaco.BlueplanetHybrid10.PvInverter+`; it has no Read-Only switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-other-special-features
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid "**Kostal PIKO** (`+Kostal.Piko.Ess+`) is only queried."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "PV inverters"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pv-inverters
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"With PV inverters, OpenEMS can set an **upper limit for the active power**. "
"With a battery inverter without PV inputs, this is the only way to limit PV "
"feed-in via OpenEMS. The upper limit is used by two functions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pv-inverters
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"**Controller.PvInverter.FixPowerLimit**: limits an inverter to a fixed value."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pv-inverters
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"**Controller.PvInverter.SellToGridLimit**: curtails the inverter so that a "
"feed-in limit is complied with at the grid connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
