"| PV part of the hybrid inverter\n"
"| Phoenix Contact\n"
"| `+PLCnext.PvInverter.Device+`\n"
"| own driver\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query only ex works"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-query-only-ex-works
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"For all PV inverters with a Read-Only setting (SMA, Fronius, Kostal, KACO "
"blueplanet, SolarEdge, Huawei, Sungrow), **Read-Only is switched on ex "
"works**. The apps in the app center (SMA, Fronius, Kostal, KACO, SolarEdge) "
"do not change this setting either. An inverter set up in this way is "
"therefore initially **only queried**. For the limitation to take effect, "
"Read-Only must be switched off in the configuration of the component."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-query-only-ex-works
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"If a function requests a limitation while Read-Only is active, it is not "
"written. The SunSpec drivers (SMA, Fronius, Kostal, KACO, SolarEdge) report "
"this via the channel `+ReadOnlyModePvLimitFailed+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query only"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-query-only
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"The following components do **not** write any setpoints or limit values to "
"the device, even if some are formally classified as controllable in OpenEMS:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Component\n"
"| Device type\n"
"\n"
"| `+Victron.PV-Inverter+`, `+Victron.PvInverter.via.DCCharger+`\n"
"| PV inverter or solar charge controller\n"
"| `+Victron.Battery-Inverter+`\n"
"| Battery inverter (control is via `+Victron.Ess+`)\n"
"| `+Kostal.Plenticore.PV-Inverter+`\n"
"| PV part of a hybrid inverter\n"
"| `+Kostal.Piko.Ess+`\n"
"| Hybrid inverter\n"
"| `+Samsung.ESS+`\n"
"| Hybrid inverter\n"
"| Bosch BPT-S 5 Hybrid\n"
"| Hybrid inverter\n"
"| `+Meter.OpenDTU+`\n"
"| Hoymiles micro-inverter via OpenDTU\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"Limitations by FixPowerLimit or SellToGridLimit and specifications from the "
"storage functions have no effect on these devices."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Special case Phoenix Contact PLCnext"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-special-case-phoenix-contact-plcnext
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"`+PLCnext.ESS.Device+` and `+PLCnext.PvInverter.Device+` connect a storage "
"or PV inverter via a PLCnext controller. Setpoints are passed to the "
"controller. Which device type is behind it depends on the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"Whether an inverter is actually controlled almost always depends on **one "
"setting**: Read-Only or control mode. It is worth checking this after setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"A **hybrid inverter** that controls itself (INTERNAL) usually needs the "
"manufacturer's meter at the grid connection. It is not required for control "
"by OpenEMS (REMOTE)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"With a **battery inverter** with a separate PV inverter, OpenEMS can only "
"limit the feed-in if the PV inverter is controllable and Read-Only is "
"switched off. Otherwise, only charging the storage remains."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"The xref:user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc[dynamic ripple "
"control receiver] only passes on its limit to GoodWe inverters. For other "
"manufacturers, the feed-in limitation must be solved differently, e.g. via "
"SellToGridLimit or directly on the inverter."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"If two systems control the same storage, for example OpenEMS and a "
"manufacturer's app or another energy management system, they work against "
"each other. Only one should be actively controlling."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/controllable-inverters.adoc
msgid ""
"Many drivers come from the community. How reliably control works in everyday "
"use depends on the respective driver and the firmware of the device."
msgstr ""
